      <p>These Terms and Conditions ("Terms") govern your use of the website and the services provided by <strong>Zusammen Tours and Travel Agency (MICE Department)</strong> ("we", "us", "our" or "Zusammen").</p>

      <p>By accessing our website, submitting an enquiry, requesting a quotation or proposal, or booking or using our services, you acknowledge that you have read, understood and agreed to these Terms and Conditions.</p>

      <h2 id="section-1">1. About Our Services</h2>

      <p>Zusammen Tours and Travel Agency (MICE Department) provides services relating to meetings, incentives, conferences and exhibitions, as well as associated travel and event services.</p>

      <p>Our services may include, but are not limited to:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Conference and meeting planning;</li>
        <li>Corporate events;</li>
        <li>Incentive travel programmes;</li>
        <li>Event and destination management;</li>
        <li>Venue sourcing and coordination;</li>
        <li>Accommodation arrangements;</li>
        <li>Airport transfers and transportation;</li>
        <li>Tours and excursions;</li>
        <li>Delegate management;</li>
        <li>Event logistics;</li>
        <li>Team-building activities;</li>
        <li>Registration and event support; and</li>
        <li>Other travel and event-related services requested by the client.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Specific services provided will depend on the client's requirements and will be confirmed in the relevant quotation, proposal, booking confirmation or service agreement.</p>

      <h2 id="section-2">2. Enquiries and Quotations</h2>

      <p>Submitting an enquiry through our website does not constitute a confirmed booking.</p>

      <p>We may provide a quotation or proposal based on the information supplied by the client.</p>

      <p>All quotations and proposals are subject to availability and may be subject to change until the booking has been confirmed in writing.</p>

      <p>Unless otherwise stated in writing, prices quoted are not guaranteed until confirmation and payment requirements have been met.</p>

      <h2 id="section-3">3. Booking Confirmation</h2>

      <p>A booking is considered confirmed only when:</p>

      <ol>
        <li>The required services have been agreed upon;</li>
        <li>The client has accepted the applicable quotation, proposal or agreement; and</li>
        <li>Any required deposit or payment has been received.</li>
      </ol>

      <p>Zusammen reserves the right to decline or cancel a booking where required payments or documentation have not been received within the agreed period.</p>

      <h2 id="section-4">4. Prices and Payments</h2>

      <p>All prices will be provided in the applicable quotation or proposal.</p>

      <p>Prices may be affected by changes in:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Accommodation rates;</li>
        <li>Venue charges;</li>
        <li>Transportation costs;</li>
        <li>Airline fares;</li>
        <li>Supplier rates;</li>
        <li>Exchange rates;</li>
        <li>Government taxes or fees;</li>
        <li>Fuel costs; and</li>
        <li>Other supplier or operational charges.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>The applicable payment schedule, deposit requirements and final payment deadline will be stated in the quotation, proposal, invoice or service agreement.</p>

      <p>The client is responsible for making payments by the agreed deadlines.</p>

      <h2 id="section-5">5. Deposits and Non-Refundable Payments</h2>

      <p>Certain suppliers, including hotels, venues, airlines, transport companies and activity providers, may require deposits or non-refundable payments.</p>

      <p>Where such conditions apply, these will be communicated to the client where reasonably possible.</p>

      <p>Payments made to secure services may be non-refundable where the relevant supplier's cancellation conditions apply.</p>

      <h2 id="section-6">6. Cancellations and Amendments</h2>

      <p>Cancellation and amendment conditions may vary depending on the services booked and the terms imposed by individual suppliers.</p>

      <p>Clients should notify Zusammen as soon as possible of any requested cancellation or amendment.</p>

      <p>Cancellation charges may include:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Supplier cancellation fees;</li>
        <li>Accommodation cancellation fees;</li>
        <li>Venue cancellation fees;</li>
        <li>Transportation cancellation fees;</li>
        <li>Airline or ticketing charges;</li>
        <li>Activity cancellation fees;</li>
        <li>Administrative charges; and</li>
        <li>Other costs incurred as a result of the cancellation or amendment.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Any refund due to the client will be subject to the applicable supplier terms and amounts actually recoverable.</p>

      <h2 id="section-7">7. Changes to an Event</h2>

      <p>Clients may request changes to an event after confirmation.</p>

      <p>Zusammen will make reasonable efforts to accommodate requested changes, subject to availability and additional costs.</p>

      <p>Changes may result in additional charges, including supplier fees, administration costs, transportation costs or changes in accommodation and venue rates.</p>

      <p>No changes are guaranteed until confirmed in writing.</p>

      <h2 id="section-8">8. Supplier Services</h2>

      <p>Zusammen may arrange services provided by independent third parties, including hotels, venues, airlines, transportation companies, restaurants, tour operators, activity providers and event suppliers.</p>

      <p>These suppliers operate under their own terms and conditions.</p>

      <p>While we take reasonable care when selecting and coordinating suppliers, we are not responsible for circumstances caused directly by a third-party supplier where such circumstances are outside our reasonable control.</p>

      <p>Where appropriate, we will assist the client in communicating with the relevant supplier and resolving service-related concerns.</p>

      <h2 id="section-9">9. Travel Documents and Requirements</h2>

      <p>Clients and delegates are responsible for ensuring that they have the necessary travel documents and comply with applicable entry requirements.</p>

      <p>Depending on the destination and circumstances, this may include:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Valid passports;</li>
        <li>Visas;</li>
        <li>Travel permits;</li>
        <li>Health or vaccination requirements;</li>
        <li>Travel insurance;</li>
        <li>Immigration requirements; and</li>
        <li>Other documents required by relevant authorities.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Zusammen may provide general travel information but does not guarantee that a client or delegate will meet the entry requirements of any country.</p>

      <p>Clients should verify applicable requirements with the relevant authorities before travelling.</p>

      <h2 id="section-10">10. Travel Insurance</h2>

      <p>We strongly recommend that clients and delegates obtain appropriate travel insurance covering circumstances such as:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Trip cancellation;</li>
        <li>Medical expenses;</li>
        <li>Emergency evacuation;</li>
        <li>Lost or damaged baggage;</li>
        <li>Travel delays;</li>
        <li>Personal liability; and</li>
        <li>Other relevant travel risks.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Unless expressly agreed in writing, travel insurance is not included in our services.</p>

      <h2 id="section-11">11. Client Responsibilities</h2>

      <p>The client agrees to:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Provide accurate and complete information;</li>
        <li>Provide required documentation within the agreed timeframes;</li>
        <li>Make payments when due;</li>
        <li>Inform us of any relevant requirements or special arrangements;</li>
        <li>Ensure that delegates comply with applicable event and supplier rules;</li>
        <li>Ensure that delegate information supplied to us is accurate; and</li>
        <li>Cooperate with reasonable requests necessary to deliver the services.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Zusammen is not responsible for problems resulting from inaccurate, incomplete or late information supplied by the client.</p>

      <h2 id="section-12">12. Delegate and Participant Information</h2>

      <p>For group events, the client may be required to provide information relating to delegates or participants.</p>

      <p>The client confirms that it has the necessary authority to provide such information to Zusammen for the purpose of delivering the requested services.</p>

      <p>Personal information will be handled in accordance with our <strong><a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a></strong>.</p>

      <h2 id="section-13">13. Special Requirements</h2>

      <p>Clients should notify us as early as possible of any special requirements, including:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Dietary requirements;</li>
        <li>Accessibility requirements;</li>
        <li>Medical or mobility considerations relevant to event arrangements;</li>
        <li>Room requirements;</li>
        <li>Transportation requirements; and</li>
        <li>Other reasonable event-related requirements.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>We will make reasonable efforts to accommodate such requests, subject to supplier availability and applicable additional costs.</p>

      <h2 id="section-14">14. Events Outside Our Control</h2>

      <p>We will not be liable for failure or delay in providing services where such failure or delay results from circumstances beyond our reasonable control.</p>

      <p>Such circumstances may include:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Natural disasters;</li>
        <li>Severe weather;</li>
        <li>Pandemics or epidemics;</li>
        <li>Government restrictions;</li>
        <li>Political unrest;</li>
        <li>Civil disturbances;</li>
        <li>War or terrorism;</li>
        <li>Strikes or industrial action;</li>
        <li>Road closures;</li>
        <li>Airline disruptions;</li>
        <li>Supplier failures;</li>
        <li>Power or telecommunications failures;</li>
        <li>Changes in laws or regulations; or</li>
        <li>Other unforeseen circumstances beyond our reasonable control.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Where such circumstances occur, we will make reasonable efforts to assist the client with alternative arrangements where possible.</p>

      <p>Additional costs arising from changes or alternative arrangements may be payable by the client.</p>

